module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.RestrictScalars
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CartesianImpliesQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentCartesianOnAffineCharts

/-!
# Generation by affine-chart sections of a module over a sheaf of algebras

Let `F` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, let
`α : 𝒪_F ⟶ A` be an arbitrary morphism from the structure sheaf of the small étale site of `F`
to a sheaf of rings `A` on that site, and let `M` be an `A`-module whose restriction of scalars
along `α` is quasi-coherent on the site.  This file proves that `M` is **generated by its
sections over an affine étale chart**, as an `A`-module: for an affine chart `V` the canonical
morphism from the free `A|_V`-module on `M(V)` to `M|_V` is an epimorphism of modules on the
slice of the small étale site at `V`.

The proof composes two results.  Quasi-coherence of the restriction of scalars
`N := (restrictScalars α).obj M` gives, by the forward implication of Descent,
Proposition 03DX(2), that `N` is cartesian on affine charts, and then
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections` generates `N|_V` by the sections of `N` over
`V`.  Since restriction of scalars does not change the underlying sheaf of abelian groups,
restricting to the slice at `V` and restricting scalars commute on the nose, so those are
already generating sections of `(restrictScalars _).obj (M.over V)`; the converse transfer of
Stacks Tag 0H88, `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.generatingSectionsOfRestrictScalars`,
then upgrades them to generating sections of `M.over V` over `A|_V`, with the same index type
and the same family of sections.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.algebraChartGeneratingSections`: the generating sections of `M.over V`
  as an `A|_V`-module, for `V` an affine étale chart.  The index type is the module `M(V)` of
  sections over the chart and the family is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mkOver`, exactly as in
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_mkOver_algebra`: the same statement in the shape
  of an epimorphism out of the free `A|_V`-module on `M(V)`.

## Implementation notes

The commutation of restriction of scalars with restriction to a slice holds by `rfl`: the two
act on different parts of the data of a sheaf of modules.  This is the site-generic form of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.restrictScalars_comp_overFunctor`, and it is used
silently — the generating sections that `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections`
produces for `N` over `V` are *already* a term of
`((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars _).obj (M.over V)).GeneratingSections`.  The morphism of
sheaves of rings on the slice is `α` pulled back along `Over.forget V`, that is
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.overPullback ... |>.map α`, written inline: the named
abbreviation `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.overHom` for the same construction is
declared only for the Zariski site of a scheme.

The topology of `A` is spelled `(smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J` rather than
`SmallEtale.topology B S hS F`, although the two are definitionally equal.  With the second
spelling the `Over V` of the slice at a `V : (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).C` carries a
category instance that instance search cannot match against the sheafification instances of the
slices, and the `HasWeakSheafify` hypothesis of
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` is then not found.

The sheafification hypotheses that Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.generatingSectionsOfRestrictScalars` carry on the
slice topology are discharged by instance search, from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleRingedSite_hasWeakSheafify_over` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleRingedSite_wEqualsLocallyBijective_over`; no new instance is
declared.

This is a step in the proof of the second assertion of Stacks Tag 08AI: the affine-chart
generation of a module that is quasi-coherent over a sheaf of algebras.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08AI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08AI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H88](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H88)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F}
    {A : Sheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J RingCat.{u}}
    (α : Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O ⟶ A)

/-- **A module over an arbitrary sheaf of algebras whose restriction of scalars is quasi-coherent
is generated by its sections over an affine étale chart**, as a module over that sheaf of
algebras.  The index type is the module `M(V)` of sections over the chart and the family of
sections is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mkOver`, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections`. -/
noncomputable def algebraChartGeneratingSections (M : SheafOfModules.{u} A)
    (hM : ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj M).IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (V : (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).C)
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V)) :
    (SheafOfModules.over M V).GeneratingSections :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.generatingSectionsOfRestrictScalars
    ((GrothendieckTopology.overPullback (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J RingCat.{u} V).map α)
    (chartGeneratingSections ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj M)
      (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF _ hM) V hV)

/-- **The same statement as an epimorphism out of a free `A|_V`-module**: the canonical morphism
from the free `A|_V`-module on the sections of `M` over an affine étale chart `V` to the
restriction `M|_V` is an epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_mkOver_algebra (M : SheafOfModules.{u} A)
    (hM : ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj M).IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (V : (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).C)
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V)) :
    Epi ((SheafOfModules.over M V).freeHomEquiv.symm
      (fun x : M.val.obj (op V) => Stacks.SheafOfModules.mkOver x)) :=
  (algebraChartGeneratingSections B S hS α M hM V hV).epi

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
